Dear GitHub customer,

<% if @is_iap %>
As you qualify for free access to GitHub Copilot Pro, your subscription benefits will now come at no cost. However, since you subscribed through an in-app purchase, you'll need to cancel your existing subscription manually to avoid future charges.

To cancel your subscription:

<% if @is_google_iap %>
For Google Play Store subscriptions:
1. Go to Google Play Store > Menu > Subscriptions
2. Find and select your GitHub Copilot subscription
3. Tap "Cancel Subscription"

For refunds: GitHub support can issue refunds for Google Play Store subscriptions. Please contact our support team at https://support.github.com/contact if you'd like to request a refund for any unused portion of your subscription.
<% else %>
For Apple App Store subscriptions:
1. Go to Settings > [Your Name] > Subscriptions on your iOS device
2. Find and select your GitHub Copilot subscription
3. Tap "Cancel Subscription"

For refunds: Apple does not allow GitHub to issue refunds for App Store subscriptions. To request a refund, you must reach out to Apple directly at https://reportaproblem.apple.com.
<% end %>

No other steps are needed to receive your free access to GitHub Copilot Pro!

<% else %>
As you qualify for free access to GitHub Copilot Pro, we recently sent you a refund receipt for your subscription. No other steps are needed to receive your free access to GitHub Copilot Pro!

Note: It may take up to 14 days for the refund to be processed by your payment provider.
<% end %>

If you have any questions about your account, please contact support at: https://support.github.com/contact.
